  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1640.03 Storage of High Explosive Materials: Class A. Table 1640.3, cited below, shall set forth the distances for storage of high explosive materials:\n\nTable 1640.3 Distances for Storage of High Explosives\n\nHIGH EXPLOSIVES | DISTANACE IN FEET WHEN STORAGE IS BARRICADED\n\n2 | 5 | 70 | 30 | 30 | 6\n\n5 | 10 | 90 | 35 | 35 | 8\n\n10 | 20 | 110 | 45 | 45 | 10\n\n20 | 30 | 125 | 50 | 50 | 11\n\n30 | 40 | 140 | 55 | 55 | 12\n\n40 | 50 | 150 | 60 | 60 | 14\n\n50 | 75 | 170 | 70 | 70 | 15\n\n75 | 100 | 190 | 75 | 75 | 16\n\n100 | 125 | 200 | 80 | 80 | 18\n\n125 | 150 | 215 | 85 | 85 | 19\n\n150 | 200 | 235 | 95 | 95 | 21\n\n200 | 250 | 255 | 105 | 105 | 23\n\n250 | 300 | 270 | 110 | 110 | 24\n\n300 | 400 | 295 | 120 | 120 | 27\n\n400 | 500 | 320 | 130 | 130 | 29\n\n500 | 600 | 340 | 135 | 135 | 31\n\n600 | 700 | 355 | 145 | 145 | 32\n\n700 | 800 | 375 | 150 | 150 | 33\n\n800 | 900 | 390 | 155 | 155 | 35\n\n900 | 1,000 | 400 | 160 | 160 | 36\n\n1,000 | 1,200 | 425 | 170 | 165 | 39\n\n1,200 | 1,400 | 450 | 180 | 170 | 41\n\n1,400 | 1,600 | 470 | 190 | 175 | 43\n\n1,600 | 1,800 | 490 | 195 | 180 | 44\n\n1,800 | 2,000 | 505 | 205 | 185 | 45\n\n2,000 | 2,500 | 545 | 220 | 190 | 49\n\n2,500 | 3,000 | 580 | 235 | 195 | 52\n\n3,000 | 4,000 | 635 | 255 | 210 | 58\n\n4,000 | 5,000 | 685 | 275 | 225 | 61\n\n5,000 | 6,000 | 730 | 295 | 235 | 65\n\n6,000 | 7,000 | 770 | 310 | 245 | 68\n\n7,000 | 8,000 | 800 | 320 | 250 | 72\n\n8,000 | 9,000 | 835 | 335 | 255 | 75\n\n9,000 | 10,000 | 865 | 345 | 260 | 78\n\n10,000 | 12,000 | 875 | 370 | 270 | 82\n\n12,000 | 14,000 | 885 | 380 | 275 | 87\n\n14,000 | 16,000 | 900 | 405 | 280 | 90\n\n16,000 | 18,000 | 940 | 420 | 285 | 94\n\n18,000 | 20,000 | 975 | 435 | 290 | 98\n\n20,000 | 25,000 | 1,055 | 470 | 315 | 105\n\n25,000 | 30,000 | 1,130 | 500 | 340 | 112\n\n30,000 | 35,000 | 1,205 | 525 | 360 | 119\n\n35,000 | 40,000 | 1,275 | 550 | 380 | 124\n\n40,000 | 45,000 | 1,340 | 570 | 400 | 129\n\nSource. #4584, eff 3-3-89; ss by #5996, INTERIM, eff 3-3-95, EXPIRES, 7-1-95; ss and moved by #6054, eff 7-1-95, EXPIRED: 7-1-03 (formerly Saf-C 1666.03)\n\nNew. #8116, INTERIM, eff 7-14-04, EXPIRES: 1-10-05; ss by #8231, eff 12-20-04; ss by #10396, eff 8-15-13\n\nAPPENDIX I\n\nRule | Material Incorporated | How Material May be Obtained\n\nSaf-C 1615.01(b) | American Table of Distances, June 1991 edition | Institute of Makers of Explosives 1120 19th Street NW, Suite 310 Washington, DC 20036-3605 Telephone: (202) 429-9280 Fax: (202) 293-2420 $15.00, excluding S&H\n\nSaf-C 1622.03(b); 1627.03; 1628.04 | Standard for Safe Havens and Interchange Lots for Vehicles Transporting Explosives, NFPA 498, (2001 Edition) effective August 2, 2001 | NFPA Headquarters address:National Fire Protection Association1 Batterymarch ParkQuincy, MA 02269Phone: 617-770-3000Fax: 617-770-0700 $33.50 (non members) and $30.15 (members); excluding S&H\n\nSaf-C 1629.08; 1631.03; 1635.08(a) | Electrical Code, NFPA 70 (2002 edition), effective April 23, 2002 | NFPA Headquarters address:National Fire Protection Association1 Batterymarch ParkQuincy, MA 02269Phone: 617-770-3000Fax: 617-770-0700 $89.50 (non members) and $80.55 (members); excluding S&H\n\nAPPENDIX II",
